   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/3792-chat-error-no-start` (head `b16a0651`, on upstream `6eb510f7`) — an error after a reply began is said alone, not as a second message.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/gateway/chat.go`'s encoder auto-started on any event (`if ev.Kind != KStart && !e.started`), and `streamError` builds its encoder from `&Request{}` — so a `KError` after the reply had begun opened a SECOND chat completion (a new `chatcmpl-…` id and a role chunk) before the error, which is what a loop cut looked like to the client.\n\n**Change.** a `KError` never auto-starts: the guard also asks `ev.Kind != KError`, so only the error event goes out, the way `streamFailure` already shaped it. The same auto-start idiom in `anthropic.go`, `responses.go` and `gemini.go` takes the same rule; #3728's keepalive start (a keepalive still opens with the model's name) is untouched, and the test that pins it stays green.\n\n**Verified.** Red: `go test -tags nogui ./internal/gateway/ -run TestLoopEndsTheReplyOnEveryProtocol` → the chat case failed with a second `chatcmpl-` id and a role delta before the error\nGreen: `same command → `ok`; the four protocols' loop tests and the keepalive start test green; the package's other tests as at base` → `ok github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gateway`\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 27's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6eb510f7` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3792-chat-error-no-start — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
